{
  "dom_id": "step-e9130",
  "name": "Example: Computing the Expected Value of a Transformed Random Variable",
  "problem": "Compute $\\textrm E[1-4X]$ if $\\textrm E[X]=\\dfrac{1}{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "For any constants $a$ and $b$ and any random variable $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[aX+b] = a \\textrm E[X]+b.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[1-4X] & =\\text{E}[-4X+1] \\\\  & =-4\\text{E}[X]+1 \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{1}{2})+1 \\\\  & =-2+1 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
